[en.EVENT_C01_C02_GREENLIGHT_34]
Battle of Ponyville

[en.EVENT_C01_C02_GREENLIGHT_34_desc]
The sun has set behind the mountains, and Ponyville may never see another sunrise.
Starlight’s army has gathered outside the village, while Trixie and her forces are stationed at the entrance, waiting for Starlight to arrive. Two former friends are about to face off in a battle that will see Ponyville lose everything it has protected for years. It is a fight with no winners, but it is also inevitable — the Empire’s reinforcements are on their way, and the vanguard has already reached the hilltop. They timed it just right, and instead of being reinforcements, they are more like referees in an arena, watching the gladiators fight, urging them on with the shrill sound of whistles.

Under the cover of darkness, Starlight’s multiple reconnaissance teams have approached Ponyville along the back roads. Starlight herself leads one of the teams, heading straight for Trixie’s residence — the wagon she will never forget, the wagon where she once shared a bed with Trixie.
Why? Why has Trixie never responded to her messages? Why has Trixie refused to work with her? Why has Trixie chosen to fight her? Starlight is still trying to convince herself that Trixie is being forced by the Empire’s surveillance, rather than truly betraying her, betraying Twilight Sparkle, betraying friendship.
But if it is all wishful thinking, can she really pull the trigger when the time comes?

For freedom, for justice, perhaps sacrifice is necessary, Starlight tells herself.

[en.EVENT_C01_C02_GREENLIGHT_34_o0]
Perhaps sacrifice is necessary.

[en.EVENT_C01_C02_GREENLIGHT_35]
Battle of Ponyville

[en.EVENT_C01_C02_GREENLIGHT_35_desc]
The Windigos circle above Ponyville, like vultures waiting for a dying animal. They have foreseen the coming conflict and eagerly await their feast on the battlefield of Ponyville.
Under the moonlight, Trixie drags her weary body away from the command post, heading towards her wagon. Along the way, she recalls how she signed the order with a quill in the war room, under the watchful eye of the Empire’s commissioner — “Find Starlight Glimmer, terminate immediately.” She thought her horn was trembling as she use magic to hold the quill, she was worried that the commissioner would notice her nervousness. But fortunately, or unfortunately, she did not tremble at all. Numb? She could no longer tell if her heart was still beating.
“To protect Ponyville, I will just pretend to cooperate with them for now.” She vaguely remembers how she whispered to the comatose Starlight Glimmer in the sickbed, but now, it is just a distant memory. How many lives has she taken, how much blood has she shed? She dare not think about it, she can only tell herself that it is all for Ponyville, for peace, for — for what?

All the prosperity of Ponyville will be gone in the night, and all the crimes she has committed over the years, will not be come redemption or protection, but destruction. When the sun rises tomorrow, all her efforts will be gone, and her name will be forever etched in the history of Ponyville — as a traitor, no matter which side wins. Or, has she really tried? Or is it just an excuse for her cowardice? Obsessed with political games, is there really any difference between her and the commissioners from Canterlot? She doesn’t know, she only knows that she can’t turn back. She is ashamed of her actions, even afraid to face Starlight, afraid to respond to Starlight’s call, even afraid to see Starlight’s face again. When Starlight left Ponyville, Trixie was not there. She could not imagine, and dared not imagine, the scene of Starlight looking at her with disappointed eyes.
Trixie does not expect her sins to be forgiven, but at least in the last moments of her life, she must prove her sincerity to Ponyville. She must fight to the very end, even if it means involving the innocent in the war, even if it means drowning her soul in the darkness, even if Starlight Glimmer sees her as a traitor. Only in this way, in the ruins of Ponyville after the war, can she preserve at least something.

If Starlight would just withdraw her troops, Ponyville would at least see another sunrise. How could Starlight not understand this?

[en.EVENT_C01_C02_GREENLIGHT_35_o0]
How could she not understand?

[en.EVENT_C01_C02_GREENLIGHT_36]
The plush toys said...

[en.EVENT_C01_C02_GREENLIGHT_36_desc]
The Operation <=Greenlight=> of the Equestria Empire built a complete system in Ponyville, including Canterlot Luxury Perfume Company and fire saftey experts.
The Equestria Empire has set up warehouses and sales points of Canterlot Luxury Perfume Company next to 17 fuel silos in Ponyville and surrounding areas. These perfumes are flammable and explosive, with hypnotic effects, and will vaporize at high temperatures, filling the entire Ponyville with flammable and hypnotic gas.
Meanwhile, the fire safety experts will create fire safety vulnerabilities in the name of “fire safety inspections” at all fuel silos in advance. In the end, a chain explosion will occur under the connection of burning perfume gas. Therefore, each “bomb” is a perfume warehouse, a fire station, a fuel silo, or some other building.
The entire operation will start from a certain “command center”, which will notify all fire safety experts and employees of Canterlot Luxury Perfume Company who can be contacted. Then they will unknowingly ignite all perfume warehouses in accordance with the employee rules and notify other sales points.

So, like all stereotypical cartoon animations, the deadly device that the evil villain uses to destroy the world always has a fatal weakness, and this weakness is — the “command center”. The Changeling Empire Central —— wait no —— the plush toys believe that this “command center” is located in Ponyville, which is the fifth “bomb”. But the plush toys do not know the specific location of the “command center”, nor do they know what it is.

[en.EVENT_C01_C02_GREENLIGHT_36_o0]
Thank you, so what is the cost?

[en.EVENT_C01_C02_GREENLIGHT_36_TOOLTIP]
Now that we know that §YBomb 5§! is the key to everything, we will prioritize the location of §YBomb 5§! when we complete §YTry to decipher the location of one “Bomb”§!.

[en.EVENT_C01_C02_GREENLIGHT_37]
Ponyville Plush Toy Subsidiary Site Selection Region Code List

[en.EVENT_C01_C02_GREENLIGHT_37_desc]
